@startuml
title sd — UC1 Select and run a finite CAN test
actor Operator
participant "GPIO/USB application adapter" as App
participant "DebouncedButtons" as Buttons
participant "ButtonTestRunner" as Runner
participant "BenchController" as Control
participant "TWAI adapter" as CAN
Operator -> App : press one button after release
loop bounded application loop
  App -> Runner : service(now), optional stop(now)
  App -> Runner : tick(now, raw mask)
  Runner -> Buttons : sample(raw mask, now)
  Buttons --> Runner : stable mask or still bouncing
  alt selection accepted while ready
    Runner -> Control : configure(bitrate), command(Start, now)
    Control -> CAN : install at selected bitrate, then start
    Control --> Runner : ready or fault
  else running and due, no pending frame
    Runner -> Control : tick with scenario frame
    Control -> CAN : submit single-shot / poll completion
    CAN --> Control : accepted, TX_SUCCESS, error or timeout
  end
  alt final completion or USB stop
    Runner -> Control : stop
    Control -> CAN : cleanup
    Control --> Runner : stopped or cleanup fault
    Runner -> Buttons : reset() — require fresh stable release
  else fault
    Runner -> Runner : latch fault, require MCU reset
  end
end
note over Runner, CAN
Same completion/error policy as existing firmware.
No queued tests or automatic retry.
No bitrate switch while controller is running.
end note
@enduml
